    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424-a1">

                <pb facs="0561" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg481"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lay to Mr.
                            Sickles.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Barcelona</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                                1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your telegram as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Pray ask for Department’s advice regarding registration of Cubans, Porto
                            Ricans and Filipinos.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sickles,</hi>”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">and letter confirming same of the 15th instant.</p>
                <p>In this connection I beg to advise you that the registration authorities in
                    Barcelona will ignore my visé on Spanish cedulas of persons born in Cuba and
                    Porto Rico who reside here, as evidence of nationality or citzenship, and they
                    are therefore not permitted to register as foreigners.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julius G. Lay</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
